{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>When you come into your fellow's vineyard.</b> Scripture speaks of one who is engaged in labor." "<b>As your soul desires.</b> As much as you wish." "<b>Your fill.</b> And not gluttonous eating (Bava Metzia 7)." "<b>But into your vessel you shall not put.</b> From here the Torah spoke only of the time of the vintage — when you would put into the vessel of the householder (Sifrei; Bava Metzia 9); but if he came to hoe and to clear away weeds, he may not eat (ibid. 7)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:09.728981881Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}